## Auto-run behavior

The UEFI shell script `startup.nsh` does the following:
- checks common USB mount locations like `fs0:` and `fs1:`
- looks for `EFI/BOOT/SREP.efi`
- looks for `SREP_Acer_AN51554.cfg` or `SREP_LOG.cfg`
- starts the EFI binary automatically
- leaves the shell open so logs can be inspected

## Recommended Acer AN515-54 BIOS steps

Before booting the USB:
- Enter BIOS with F2 or Del
- Set Boot Mode to UEFI
- Disable Secure Boot
- Disable Fast Boot if present
- Ensure USB is above internal drives in boot order
- Save changes and reboot

## Config usage

The sample config file is intentionally a safe template.

Edit `SREP_Acer_AN51554.cfg` before using it in production. Replace placeholder commands with actual firmware patterns, GUIDs, and offsets from your BIOS image.

Example structure:
```ini
Op Loaded
SetupUtility

Op FastestPatch
Offset
0x1234
AABBCCDD

Op End
```

Use the upstream project docs for command syntax:
https://github.com/Maxinator500/SmokelessRuntimeEFIPatcher-RUS/blob/master/README.md

## Recovery / rollback

If a patch breaks booting:
- power off and unplug AC
- hold power button for 30 seconds
- reinsert battery if accessible and CMOS reset if required
- boot into BIOS recovery / Acer BIOS recovery mode

## Safe workflow

1. Download SREP
2. Create USB
3. Boot with logging enabled
4. Confirm config loads and no errors appear
5. Add one small patch at a time
6. Review `SREP.log` after each run
7. Only keep working patches

